# Which of this deployment's services run in a container of their own, and
# what each may use. Copy to var/containers.conf and uncomment a line to move
# that service; var/, because the figures belong to one machine.
#
# A service with a line here starts in its container (scripts/run-service.sh,
# README "Services in containers"). A service with no line starts natively.
# Removing a line and reinstalling the service moves it back.
#
# Both limits, always. A container given neither gets 4 CPUs and 1 GiB
# whatever the service is, so a line that states only one of them is refused
# by name. CPUs are a whole number; memory is a number and M or G, and
# Apple's container refuses less than 200M.
#
# The figures below are places to start: set each from what the service is
# seen to use on this machine. One is measured (design/measured.md,
# 2026-11-24): the hourly projection's shape, three days in one run with
# trades and quotes for nine instruments, peaked at 8.2 GiB in a container,
# and a lane given 4G was killed, not slowed. A day captured since holds no
# trades, and needs somewhat less.
#
# service              cpus  memory
# flows                  4     12G
# nats                   1     256M
# capture:hyperliquid    2     1G
# ledger:hyperliquid     2     2G
